I built One Card Tarot (<a href="https://onecardtarot.org" rel="nofollow">https://onecardtarot.org</a>
), a simple web app that gives instant, one-card tarot readings with AI-generated interpretations.<p>The idea came from noticing that most tarot apps are either:<p>Overwhelming (full spreads, long rituals), or<p>Too generic (static meanings with no context)<p>I wanted something closer to how many people actually use tarot day to day:
ask one clear question, draw one card, and reflect.<p>What it does<p>Ask a question (or draw without one)<p>Draw one random tarot card (upright or reversed)<p>Get an AI-powered interpretation tailored to:<p>Love &amp; relationships<p>Yes / No questions<p>Daily guidance &amp; reflection<p>Free users get limited daily readings, and there are optional paid plans for heavier use.<p>Why one card?<p>From my own experience, one-card tarot is:<p>Faster<p>Easier to reflect on<p>Less likely to turn into over-analysis<p>The constraint actually makes the interpretation more interesting.<p>Tech stack (high level)<p>Next.js<p>Serverless APIs<p>AI-generated interpretations (prompted to stay concise and grounded)<p>Stripe for payments<p>No accounts required to try it.<p>What I’m looking for<p>Feedback on the UX and interpretation quality<p>Thoughts on whether AI adds real value here or not<p>Suggestions for features that don’t make it more complicated<p>Happy to answer questions or share implementation details if useful.<p>Thanks!

